Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.43,0:00:05.30,Default,,0,0,0,,If a coin is hidden inside a box you may not know\Nwhether it shows heads or tails That
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.31,0:00:10.10,Default,,0,0,0,,lack of knowledge is not the same as quantum\Nsuperposition To describe a qubit we use
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.11,0:00:14.97,Default,,0,0,0,,amplitudes They determine outcome probabilities and also\Ncarry a relationship called
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.98,0:00:20.40,Default,,0,0,0,,phase This phase will matter when the amplitudes\Ninterfere A state can offer equal
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.41,0:00:25.22,Default,,0,0,0,,chances of zero and one but other states can have\Ndifferent probabilities It is not
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.23,0:00:28.90,Default,,0,0,0,,correct to say that every qubit always has a fifty\Npercent chance of each result
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.63,0:00:32.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Everything depends on preparation and on how we measure